‘The state should limit rents because families on low incomes will otherwise be forced out of their neighbourhoods – like the family that could no longer find an affordable home when they needed to move.’ {{1}}
‘Price caps are simply a stupid idea.’ {{2}}
‘A price cap below the equilibrium price leads to shortages because more is demanded than supplied – in several countries, shelves for products with capped prices were empty.’ {{3}}
‘Without rent controls, rents will keep rising.’ {{4}}
‘Having a public authority check electricity network charges protects customers because there is no competition – the network belongs to a single supplier.’ {{5}}
‘Every sensible person is against price caps.’ {{6}}
‘Rent controls can slow down housebuilding because building becomes less profitable – critics point to cities with strict rules and little new housing.’ {{7}}
‘Price caps prevent profiteering in crises because desperate people will otherwise pay almost any price – for example, for drinking water after a disaster.’ {{8}}
‘High prices often regulate themselves because they attract new suppliers and curb demand – a cap switches off this signal.’ {{9}}
‘Politicians should finally start being sensible about this issue.’ {{10}}
